.TH HOP-TUNES 1 "October 2026" "hop-tunes 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hop-tunes \- a local-first music player
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hop-tunes
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-forget\-pin\fR \fIPROFILE\fR] [\fIFILE\fR|\fIFOLDER\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Hop-tunes plays the music files you already own. It works fully offline: there are no
accounts, no sign-in and no tracking. Several people can share one computer through local
profiles, each with its own music folders, playlists, history and settings.
.PP
Files and folders named on the command line start playing straight away, even if they are
not in your music folders. If Hop-tunes is already running, they are sent to that window
instead of opening a second one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-forget\-pin " PROFILE"
Remove a forgotten PIN from the named profile, then exit. Nothing else in the profile changes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/hop-tunes/shared/index.sqlite
Track index shared by all profiles (tags and audio properties; safe to delete, it is rebuilt).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/hop-tunes/profiles/
One folder per profile: settings, playlists, play counts, history.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/hop-tunes/
Cover art cache (safe to delete).
.PP
In the Flatpak these live under \fI~/.var/app/io.github.thestylewithin.Hop-tunes/\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOPTUNES_PLAYBIN
Set to \fBplaybin\fR to use GStreamer's classic playback engine instead of playbin3.
.SH NOTES
Hop-tunes never changes, moves or uploads your music files. A profile PIN is a privacy
curtain, not security: anyone who can use your computer account can read Hop-tunes' files.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project page: https://github.com/theStyleWithin/Hop-tunes
